Ways to reduce the constant adjusting:

Use hysteresis on contact
Only drop a finger after it has been “not in contact” for N steps. This avoids flickering.
Don’t zero out actuators entirely
Instead of removing non‑contact fingers from the solve, keep them but down‑weight them. That keeps the solution stable.
Freeze Jacobian updates when contact is low
When c_filtered drops, stop updating J for a few frames. Otherwise you chase noisy data.
Increase regularization when contact is low
You already do some of this. Increase it further so the solution doesn’t jump.
Cap how much delta_q can change per step
You already clip, but you can make it stricter so the grasp doesn’t “fidget.”

